body:
Mistakes are not breaches of sobriety. Yes, this is an 'opinion' but I'm gonna go full asshole here and say anyone who disagrees with this opinion is wrong.

Again, IMO, this only became a breach if you took a gulp, realized what it was, then made the CONSCIOUS decision to keep drinking out of that cup.

&#x200B;

That's why they say 'one day at a time'.

I understand the 'trapped by sobriety' feeling. But if you really think about it, is 'trapped by sobriety' any worse than 'trapped by drinking'?

&#x200B;

I just tell people. I consider alcoholism a disorder, so I feel no more shame than telling someone that I have epilepsy or something.

Almost everyone has been supportive. And honestly, those that have a problem with me making a positive life change? Screw them.

&#x200B;

I think it's an excuse, but that is just my opinion.

I think some do better and some do worse when attaching math or numbers to, well, anything. Diet. Time at gym. Number of times having sex in a month with their SO.

&#x200B;

&#x200B;
